WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.850
Hi! Today we'll meet three four-sided shapes: the parallelogram, the rhombus and the trapezium, and use their properties to find angles.

2
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:21.690
A parallelogram has two pairs of opposite sides. Each pair is parallel and equal in length. The arrows show which sides are parallel.

3
00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:29.778
Its opposite angles are equal. This angle is 70 degrees, so the opposite angle is also 70 degrees.

4
00:00:29.928 --> 00:00:42.450
Two angles next to each other, between a pair of parallel lines, add up to 180 degrees. So the other two angles are 180 minus 70, which is 110 degrees.

5
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:51.042
A rhombus is a special parallelogram with all four sides the same length. The angle facts are the same.

6
00:00:51.192 --> 00:00:55.362
A trapezium has only one pair of parallel sides.

7
00:00:55.512 --> 00:01:02.370
The two angles on the same slanted side, between the parallel lines, add up to 180 degrees.

8
00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:13.386
The bottom angle is 65 degrees, so the top angle is 180 minus 65, which is 115 degrees.

9
00:01:13.536 --> 00:01:19.818
One more: a rhombus has an angle of 52 degrees. What are the other three angles?

10
00:01:19.968 --> 00:01:30.402
Angles next to each other add up to 180 degrees, so the next one is 180 minus 52, which is 128 degrees.

11
00:01:30.552 --> 00:01:44.298
Opposite angles are equal, so the four angles are 52, 128, 52 and 128 degrees. They add up to exactly 360 degrees.

12
00:01:44.448 --> 00:01:51.498
Watch out! Some pupils think a trapezium's opposite angles are equal too. That is wrong!

13
00:01:51.648 --> 00:02:02.658
Only parallelograms and rhombuses have equal opposite angles. For a trapezium, use the two angles on the same slanted side, which add up to 180 degrees.

14
00:02:02.808 --> 00:02:07.794
Before you start, check which sides are parallel.

15
00:02:07.944 --> 00:02:20.082
Your turn! A parallelogram has an angle of 118 degrees. What are the other three angles? Pause and think.

16
00:02:20.232 --> 00:02:35.346
The angle next to it is 180 minus 118, which is 62 degrees. So the other three angles are 62, 118 and 62 degrees. Did you get it right?

17
00:02:35.496 --> 00:02:49.434
Another one! In a trapezium, the bottom angle on one slanted side is 72 degrees. What is the angle above it on the same side? Pause and think.

18
00:02:49.584 --> 00:03:01.746
The two angles on the same slanted side add up to 180 degrees. 180 minus 72 is 108 degrees. Did you get it right?

19
00:03:01.896 --> 00:03:16.866
Remember: in parallelograms and rhombuses, opposite angles are equal and angles next to each other add up to 180 degrees. In a trapezium, the two angles on the same slanted side add up to 180 degrees.

20
00:03:17.016 --> 00:03:21.210
Now go and practise in your garden!

